      "id": "bbc-2026-07-25-heatwave-conditions-to-return-for-many-as-uk-temperatures-to",
      "title": "Heatwave conditions to return for many as UK temperatures to peak at 35C",
      "summary": "Following weeks of mainly dry weather, we can welcome some rain this weekend, but it is not going to be that much.",
      "body": "For most of England and Wales the third heatwave of the year ended last weekend when cooler air arrived, dropping maximum temperatures widely to 20-24C.However, two locations - Usk and Exeter - have continued to just reach their heatwave criteria since then and have now reached 20 consecutive days - the longest run so far this year.As temperatures drop further over the weekend, and parts of the UK see a little rain, even these local heatwaves are likely to come to an end.However, it may only be a temporary break.Next week, high pressure is set to build close to the south of the UK meaning rain-bearing weather fronts will stall.Any wet weather will become confined to northern and western areas - especially north-west Scotland - and in southern parts of the UK temperatures look set to climb once again.This could well mean a fourth heatwave is on the cards - although according to the Met Office isolated high temperatures might not be enough.They say that: \"If only one or two stations reach heatwave criteria, that would not be defined as a heatwave.\"",
