      "id": "bbc-2026-07-24-officers-hurt-as-police-boat-hits-westminster-bridge",
      "title": "Officers hurt as police boat hits Westminster Bridge",
      "summary": "Police say a number of armed officers entered the River Thames but were recovered after the crash.",
      "body": "Mother and son Cecilia Lusevic, 56, and Mateo Bilis-Lusevic, 12, said they heard a loud bang when the police boat crashed into Westminster Bridge and then watched as the officers were rescued from the River Thames.The visitors from Chile were on a river tour boat on the north side of the central London bridge when they saw the incident. They were evacuated from their vessel shortly after.Mateo said: \"Two boats were riding extremely fast through the water.\"Suddenly, I heard a boom. I was looking towards the boat, and I heard a boom.\"Then three people went flying into the water and one of the people was really hurt.\"He said the officers were in the water for about 10 minutes and a life ring was thrown for one of them.A black rigid inflatable boat arrived to help them out of the water  – the same boat that witnesses said they saw paramedics treating the casualties aboard.Mateo said emergency services then also arrived.A London Ambulance Service spokesperson said it sent ambulance crews, incident response officers, and paramedic teams as well as London's Air Ambulance to the incident. London Fire Brigade said it deployed a fire boat and three fire rescue units with water rescue capabilities to the scene.Listen to the best of BBC Radio London on Sounds and follow BBC London on Facebook, external, X, external and Instagram, external. Send your story ideas to hello.bbclondon@bbc.co.uk, external",
