      "id": "techcrunch-2026-07-22-google-is-making-it-easier-to-switch-from-iphone-to-android",
      "title": "Google is making it easier to switch from iPhone to Android",
      "summary": "The new feature lets users wirelessly transfer more data types from an iPhone without needing to download a separate app.",
      "body": "10:08 AM PDT · July 22, 2026\nGoogle announced on Wednesday a new migration experience built directly into Android 17 that should ease the switch from iPhone to Android. The feature lets users wirelessly transfer more data types from an iPhone without needing to download a separate app, Google says.\nBy simplifying the onboarding process and supporting more data types, the tech giant is looking to lower the barriers to switching smartphone ecosystems as it aims to attract more iPhone users.\nWith this new method, users can transfer photos, videos, contacts, messages, calendars, and newly supported data types, including their Google Account, passwords, Wi-Fi credentials, and even their eSIM, when switching from an iPhone to Android.\nThe upgrade has already started rolling out to select Pixel devices, and it’s also available on the  new Samsung Galaxy Z Flip8 and Z Fold8 series, which were unveiled today. The new migration method will also come to more Android devices soon, Google says.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Aisha Malik",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-22T17:08:03.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-22-at-12.32.37-PM.png?resize=1200,669",
