      "id": "bbc-2026-07-22-the-global-story-is-the-iran-war-back-on",
      "title": "The Global Story: Is the Iran war back on?",
      "summary": "The White House has asked Congress for billions more dollars in funding for the Iran war",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsWorld Service,·22 Jul 2026,·27 minsAvailable for over a yearThe US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth faced senators on Tuesday as the White House asked for tens of billions of dollars more to help fund the Iran war.\nIt comes after over a week of consecutive US strikes, the deaths of several US service members, and the Iran-backed Houthis announcing a ‘maritime blockade’ in the region.\nWe speak to BBC world news correspondent Joe Inwood about the trouble brewing on three fronts for the US.\nProducers: Sam Chantarasak and Valerio Esposito\nSenior news editor: China Collins\nPhoto: A projectile is fired during what the U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) said was a round of strikes against Iran, in this screen grab taken from a handout video released on July 11, 2026. Credit: U.S. Central Command/Handout/Reuters.Programme WebsiteMore episodes",
