      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-22-show-hn-a-new-kind-of-fps-aim-trainer",
      "title": "Show HN: A new kind of FPS aim trainer",
      "summary": "I played a lot of Valorant and got mad, so I made an aim trainer that analyzes your raw crosshair movement to explore your raw motor and perceptual weaknesses instead of scoring scenarios.\nIt also chooses sens and difficulty as part of the tasks, and makes playlists that are optimal difficulty for you to learn and progress faster!\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49002276\nPoints:",
      "body": "Target colorPresets are colorblind-friendly against every theme.\nArena moodEarned backdrop palettes — free play only. Locked ones show what unlocks them.\nTarget finishEarned target skins — free play only. Rated drills always use the standard target.\nLiving sceneBackdrop shifts between drills & drifts slowly to fight visual fatigue. Never touches targets or contrast.\nReduced eye strainDims & warms the scene and UI for long sessions — lowers luminance load. Targets keep full contrast.\nMotionReduce disables UI transitions; Auto follows your OS.\nOutlineKeeps the crosshair visible over targets.\nOn-target reactionOff by default for clean telemetry.\nMiss flashRed flick at the crosshair on a missed shot.\nShot feedback soundsMissed shots and magazine reloads.\nBlocked-shot cueMulti-tap drills cap the fire rate. Marks pulls that came too early to fire, so they read as your timing, not lag.\nTracking toneSustained lock tone that climbs while your crosshair holds a target.\nOff-screen spawn cuePanned alert pointing to targets that spawn out of view.\nOff-screen spawn markerA brief edge chevron toward a target that spawns out of view — the visual twin of the spawn cue.\nPace metronomeCoached drills: one beat per pace budget.\nReward momentsConfetti + a flourish when you set a record, rank up, or hit a streak.\nEye-rest remindersA gentle 20-20-20 nudge between drills on long sessions.\nZen modeHide the whole HUD during runs; results still show everything.\nMouse DPIOptional. Enables cm/360 and hand-travel modeling.\nImport sensConverts your in-game sensitivity.\nField of viewHorizontal; stamped into every replay.\nRaw inputWhether the browser delivers unaccelerated mouse motion. OpenAim never accelerates; this is the browser/OS layer.\nChallenge pointTarget success rate drills are solved to.\nExplanationsFull detail always stays behind the ? chip.\nSession lengthDrills per coached session.\nFocusLet the coach choose, or lock the session to one axis.\nAutoGainSens auto-tuning from measured under/overshoot.\nCapture levelSummary skips raw mouse/camera streams; deep analysis needs Full.\nAuto-download replaySave the .oar after every completed run.\nAnonymous drill summaries are contributed by default to train the shared,\nscience-based player model everyone starts from and that renormalizes your ratings\nto real peers. No raw mouse traces, no identity, no device info — and you can opt out\nor revoke below anytime. Raw replays and the public leaderboard stay off unless you\nContribute runsSends drill summaries + capability features (no raw mouse, no device info) to sharpen the population model everyone starts from.\nLeaderboardRank on the task-Elo boards under a public handle.\nShare replaysAdvanced: uploads raw mouse-movement traces (mildly biometric) for deeper analysis and spectating. Requires the two above.\nSettings that change the meaning of telemetry (FOV, sens, target style, crosshair, invert, capture level)\nare recorded in each replay's .oar header, so analysis reflects the settings the run used.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "pmazumder",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-22T05:39:31.000Z",
