      "id": "bbc-2026-07-22-burnham-pulls-back-on-suggestion-to-increase-tax-free-person",
      "title": "Burnham pulls back on suggestion to increase tax-free personal allowance",
      "summary": "Burnham has previously said that the freeze in the tax allowance was a big issue in the Makerfield by-election",
      "body": "Andy Burnham has pulled back from suggestions about increasing the tax-free personal allowance.The £12,570 threshold has been frozen since 2021, resulting in more people being dragged into paying tax as earnings increase.Burnham told the Times over the weekend that the \"frustration about the personal allowance\" he had heard while campaigning in the Makerfield by-election was \"lodged in my mind\".The prime minister then told reporters on Monday that \"all of this will be looked at\" in the next budget but conceded any change would be expensive and \"difficult given the financial circumstances in which we find ourselves\".Those close to Burnham have since told BBC News that any changes to the personal allowance are not part of his initial plan to tackle the cost of living.It comes after Burnham told his first cabinet meeting: \"We've got to show fiscal discipline. We've got to show that our commitment to the fiscal rules is real and we're prepared to make difficult decisions in relation to that.\"Burnham has committed to Labour's 2024 manifesto, which included a promise not to increase the basic, higher, or additional rates of income tax.That would rule out increasing the top rate of income tax paid by higher earners to offset the cost of lifting the personal allowance.The Institute for Fiscal Studies has estimated that unfreezing the threshold could end up costing £8.5-9bn a year.Burnham said on Monday that he was \"just kind of showing I have visibility of the issue and the impact it's had.\"He told reporters it would be \"looked at\" in the Budget, but added: \"Obviously it's difficult, given the financial circumstances in which we find ourselves.\"Government sources told the Telegraph on Tuesday that there were \"no plans\" to announce any changes to the £12,570 personal allowance \"in the short term\".",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-22T01:43:54.000Z",
