      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-21-show-hn-computable-buy-sell-and-redeem-gpu-for-the-exact-wee",
      "title": "Show HN: Computable – Buy, sell, and redeem GPU for the exact weeks you want",
      "summary": "Hey we are Computable. We spent years building trading infrastructure at Jump Trading and Coinbase. From that point of view, compute looks like energy markets before 2000: everything trades through private bilateral leases, there’s no visible price, and nothing can be resold. The same H100 rents at a 2x spread depending on who’s asking, and once you sign a 24-month lease, it can never change hands",
      "body": "Computable is the first and only place where you can easily buy, sell, and redeem GPU hours across calendar weeks, with instant liquidity.\nRental marketplaces charge extra for that flexibility, but our hours come at wholesale with the freedom to sell what you don't use.\nBuy GPU hoursTHE HOURS YOU NEED, ANY WEEKS ON THE CALENDAR\nFounders from Jump Trading and Coinbase\nAUGUST THROUGH JANUARY · SOLD BY THE WEEK\nWe're auctioning a cluster of GPU nodes, August through next January, sold by the week. A bid is a flexible shape: how many nodes, which weeks, your price. Sealed, pay what you bid, and every clearing price gets published after settlement. Bidding is open now and closes July 31.\nJoin the AuctionSEALED UNTIL CLOSE · JULY 31\nPay for only the weeks you need.\nPick two nodes for the last two weeks of October, pay for exactly those, and walk away when the run is done.\nSell back what you don't use.\nWe keep a standing buyback quote posted on every position, so unused capacity turns back into cash the moment you hit sell.\nYou can buy (or sell) the future.\nLock January in July at a price you set, so you know exactly what the future run costs in case another H100 40% rate jump happens.",
