      "id": "bbc-2026-07-21-bournemouth-reject-64m-bid-from-chelsea-for-scott",
      "title": "Bournemouth reject £64m bid from Chelsea for Scott",
      "summary": "Bournemouth reject a £64m bid from Chelsea for Alex Scot after the midfielder turns down a new contract amid growing Premier League interest.",
      "body": "Bournemouth have rejected a £64m bid from Chelsea for midfielder Alex Scott.The Cherries made it clear to the Blues that any further approaches would not be welcomed and that they intend to keep hold of one of their star players. However, it remains a difficult situation for the club as the England Under-21 international has rejected a new contract that has been on the table for at least two months. Arsenal, Manchester United, Tottenham and Manchester City also expressed an interest in Scott earlier in the window. BBC Sport reported in June that Arsenal had an approach for Scott turned down by Bournemouth.The 22-year-old, who joined Bournemouth from Bristol City in 2023 for £25m, has two years left on his current deal.Bournemouth have insisted publicly, directly to the player and to interested clubs that he will remain on the south coast, even on that current contract.The south coast club are under no pressure to sell after qualifying for the Europa League and generating significant income through the sales last summer of Dean Huijsen, Milos Kerkez, Illia Zabarnyi and Dango Outtara.They have taken a similar stance with highly rated forward Junior Kroupi, who is attracting interest from Arsenal and Tottenham.Brazil international Rayan is also not expected to leave and has given no indication that he wants to, having only joined the club in January.",
