      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-21-incremental-a-library-for-incremental-computations",
      "title": "Incremental – A library for incremental computations",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://github.com/janestreet/incremental\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48987822\nPoints: 263\n# Comments: 50",
      "body": "Incremental is a library that gives you a way of building complex\ncomputations that can update efficiently in response to their inputs\nchanging, inspired by the work of Umut Acar et. al. on self-adjusting\ncomputations. Incremental can be useful in a number of applications,\nBuilding large calculations (of the kind you might build into a\nspreadsheet) that can react efficiently to changing data.\nConstructing views in GUI applications that can incorporate new data\nComputing derived data while guaranteeing that the derived data\nstays in sync with the source data, for instance filtering or\nYou can find detailed documentation of the library and how to use\nit in incremental/src/incremental_intf.ml.  You can also find an\ninformal introduction to the library in this blog post",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "handfuloflight",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-21T03:50:53.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://opengraph.githubassets.com/a73eb7307cd0b91443487221d2f7310e3c30fd072d5189da8f862731b3b7bfea/janestreet/incremental",
      "originalUrl": "https://github.com/janestreet/incremental",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
