      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-20-claude-fable-produced-a-counterexample-to-the-jacobian-conje",
      "title": "Claude Fable produced a counterexample to the Jacobian Conjecture",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://xcancel.com/__alpoge__/status/2079028340955197566\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48973869\nPoints: 355\n# Comments: 204",
      "body": "hello there the jacobian conjecture is false thanx to my close friend akhil for asking about it and my other close friend fable for working during the world cup final\n((1+xy)^3 z + y^2 (1+xy) (4+3xy), y + 3 x (1+xy)^2  z + 3 x y^2 (4+3xy), 2 x - 3 x^2 y - x^3 z): \\C^3\\to \\C^3, has jacobian determinant -2, and sends (0, 0, -1/4), (1, -3/2, 13/2), and (-1, 3/2, 13/2) to (-1/4, 0, 0)\nJul 20, 2026 · 2:19 AM UTC\nI asked Fable to rank the 50 most important unsolved math problems and this one ranked 23rd!\nMe asking google what the 23rd letter is for u\nThank you blessed math fairy\nliz we both know @gork would know better\nMy face when about to click post on this one..\nYo he is so incredible. i was at his first talk on small gaps:D the story was that he relied on a result which had a gap right\ninvesting at 0 likes in case this is true\nThis is the most hilarious / horrifying problem because it is like the canonical crank graveyard. Ty 4 investment🙏\nmaybe a stupid question, but doesnt this also imply that dixmier conjecture and poisson conjecture are false in general?\nYea i think so. i was considering tweeting it too but people know jacobian much better..\nfable is 180 iq, confirmed by my trusted advisor\nframe this tweet in the louvre\nNice. But I have the impression that people really cared about dimension 2. Is there a similar example in that case ?\nfable would rename it \"the World Cup map\" lmao\nUghhh! My AG heart can’t take this! It’s fine. Stay strong. The Jacobian Conjecture has survived worse!!!\nkimi agreed  This is now extremely interesting: three fully independent verifications (symbolic expansion, numerical finite differences, and exact rational arithmetic with hand-derived partial derivatives) all confirm both halves of the claim:\ndet JF ≡ −2 everywhere (a nonzero constant), and\nF(0,0,−1/4) = F(1,−3/2,13/2) = F(−1,3/2,13/2) = (−1/4,0,0) — so F is genuinely non-injective.\nThe absolute state of maths.\nThe displayed collision is not isolated. For every (r\\in\\mathbb C^\\times),\nThus there is a 1-parameter family of triple fibers; as (r\\to\\infty), two preimages escape to infinity while the image tends to (0).\nEh, I remember when a Prof in my undergrad AG class discussed it at the end of the semester in a class where we were covering some fun topics after being done with coursework. He described it then as a simple to state but profound in consequences and we were all dreaming of disproving it with a simple counterexample. Now we're all the way here. Big congrats.",
