      "id": "techcrunch-2026-07-18-federal-employees-can-download-tiktok-on-their-work-phones-a",
      "title": "Federal employees can download TikTok on their work phones again",
      "summary": "The Department of Justice says that federal employees can now download TikTok on their government devices.",
      "body": "8:54 AM PDT · July 18, 2026\nImage Credits:Jaap Arriens/NurPhoto / Getty Images\nThe Department of Justice says that federal employees can now download TikTok on their government devices, according to Reuters.\nA 2022 law banned federal employees from using the short-form video app on those devices, but the DOJ reportedly says the law no longer applies, thanks to a deal transferring ownership of TikTok’s U.S. operations to a joint venture backed by Oracle, Silver Lake, and MGX. (Oracle serves as the security partner for the new joint venture, while previous owner ByteDance retains a 19.9% stake.)\nThe DOJ memo reportedly says President Donald Trump has cleared “employees of Executive Branch agencies” to “download TikTok onto their official devices, subject ​to the agency’s discretion and consistent with all applicable workplace policies.”\nFollowing the ban focused on government employees and devices, the app was banned more broadly across the United States. But just as the law took effect early last year, the app only went down briefly before Trump repeatedly delayed the move and urged service providers to restore access.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news\nLatest in Government & Policy",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
