    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-18-drdroid-yc-w23-is-hiring",
      "title": "DrDroid (YC W23) Is Hiring",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/drdroid/jobs/w45QcNV-product-engineer-assignment-mandatory\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48954074\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Your best friend in production.Product Engineer [Assignment mandatory]₹1.7M - ₹2.1M INR•0.01% - 0.10%•Bengaluru, KA, IN / Bengaluru, Karnataka, INRoleEngineering, Full stackVisaUS citizenship/visa not requiredSkillsJavaScript, Python, TypeScriptConnect directly with founders of the best YC-funded startups.Apply to role ›About the roleAbout the interview\nAssignment as per this doc - mandatory\nExpect all of this in less than 7 days from the date of assignment submission.\nDrDroid is building AI Agents for Platform & Infrastructure teams.\nWe help engineering teams fix issues faster and reduce escalations during on-call—automating triage, debugging, and remediation.\nWe’re also the team behind several open-source projects:\n🔹 Playbooks – A runbook automation platform\n🔹 Kenobi – An event analytics platform for debugging data pipelines\nJoin us in redefining how teams run operations in the post-GPT world.\nThink if anyone in the team can debug an average production issue without requiring to involve a senior engineer (or a team of engineers?). Wouldn't that be wonderful? That's what we are working towards.\nTo work towards our vision, we couldn’t have been more grateful for having some amazing investors. We are lucky enough to be supported by Accel and we were part of Y-Combinator’s W23 batch.\nIn case you are interested to know more about the team, check this page. If you're passionate about building tools to improve lives of other developers, we might be a good fit.",
